KNOWLEDGE

Files user uploaded to workspace. User sees same files in sidebar; every
change shows there at once.

- (knowledge/list) lists file names, like "report.md".
- (knowledge/read "name") by extension: .ptc gives its one form as data, never
  run; .json gives JSON as data, object as alist; .pdf gives page text as
  string; other text gives string. Other binary (image) refused. nil when no
  file.
- (knowledge/write "name" value) replaces file; user can open and download it.
  User approves it. .ptc takes data, printed; function refused. .json takes
  data, written as JSON: plist or alist becomes object, other list becomes
  array, keyword becomes its name; or takes JSON text string. Other file takes
  string.
- Edit .ptc file: read, change with set-in / update-in / remove-in, write back:
  (knowledge/write "notes.ptc" (set-in (knowledge/read "notes.ptc") "done" :status))
- (knowledge/delete "name") removes file. User approves it.

BIN

Files user attached to message land in bin, shown as bin/ in sidebar. Bin
files expire after a week unless kept.

- User message can point at file: @knowledge/report.md or @bin/spec.pdf;
  quoted when name has space: @"bin/Q3 Sales.json". Read it with
  (knowledge/read "report.md") or (bin/read "spec.pdf"), name without folder.
- (bin/list) lists bin file names.
- (bin/read "name") reads bin file, same rules as knowledge/read.
- (knowledge/keep "name") moves bin file into knowledge, kept for good. Keep
  what user wants to reuse later; leave rest to expire.
- (bin/write "name" value) puts file in bin. String stored as text;
  (:base64 "…" :type "image/png") stored as bytes, like image from tool.
  Returns stored name; gains number when name taken.
- (bin/fetch "https://…") downloads url into bin; (bin/fetch url "name")
  names it. User approves it. Returns stored name.
